From e275c3dc70e1c2947e02e43aeee6c4f9975c3dc7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ramasamy Kaliappan <ramasamy.kaliappan@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Thu, 25 Sep 2025 15:55:11 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] AP MLD: Deinitialize BSS link on interface setup failure

Fix a segmentation fault in hostapd when interface setup fails in
hostapd_add_iface() due to invalid channel information. In this case,
the driver is deinitialized but the BSS link is not, leading to a crash
when the interface is brought down and up during stability testing.

Deinitialize the BSS link if interface setup fails to ensure proper
cleanup and prevent the crash.

[Petr: Adjust hunk context for the older driver_init() error check,
which has no braces.]

Signed-off-by: Ramasamy Kaliappan <ramasamy.kaliappan@oss.qualcomm.com>
Signed-off-by: Aaradhana Sahu <aaradhana.sahu@oss.qualcomm.com>
Signed-off-by: Petr Štetiar <petr.stetiar@prplfoundation.org>
(cherry picked from commit e275c3dc70e1c2947e02e43aeee6c4f9975c3dc7)
---
 src/ap/hostapd.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/ap/hostapd.c b/src/ap/hostapd.c
index 94ff2aae9b8f..0ee85bc91d82 100644
--- a/src/ap/hostapd.c
+++ b/src/ap/hostapd.c
@@ -4014,6 +4014,8 @@
 				goto fail;
 
 			if (hostapd_setup_interface(hapd_iface)) {
+				/* Deinit link for the first bss */
+				hostapd_bss_link_deinit(hapd_iface->bss[0]);
 				hostapd_deinit_driver(
 					hapd_iface->bss[0]->driver,
 					hapd_iface->bss[0]->drv_priv,
-- 
